IMPORT prelude

-- Online Safety (Relief and Accountability) Act 2025 (Singapore) -- who may report an online harm to the Commissioner of Online
-- Safety (ss 4, 22, 25), when only a right of reply may be ordered (s 26(5), (6)), selected definitions of the online harmful
-- activities (ss 9, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 19(4), 20), the offences of non-compliance and their maxima (ss 69, 71, 72, 73), the
-- statutory torts against the person who did it (ss 83 to 88), the duty of a group or forum administrator to answer an online harm
-- notice (ss 89, 91, 92; s 94 for online service providers is parallel), enhanced damages (s 98), where the tort takes place
-- (s 101), contract terms excluding liability (s 102) and starting a Part 10 claim in the Family Court (s 106).
--
-- Edition: Act 23 of 2025, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/OSRAA2025.txt. Every page of the
-- deposit is footed "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 29/6/2026"; no amending Act or subsidiary legislation is
-- annotated in it. The deposit does not say which Parts are in operation: s 1(1) leaves commencement to Gazette notification, and
-- ss 3(1), 89(1) and 93(1) exclude "an activity the definition of which in Part 3 has not been brought into operation".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: anyone who is harassed, doxxed, stalked,
-- impersonated or deepfaked online, or whose intimate images are shared, meets it, as does anyone who runs a chat group or forum.
-- SCOPED. Not encoded: the Commissioner and Appeal Panel and reconsideration and appeals (Parts 2 and 7), the content of each Part 5 direction and order
-- (ss 29 to 47), information and end-user identity powers (Part 6), corporate liability, composition and the remedial initiative
-- (ss 74 to 78), s 90 (facilitating harm at an online location) beyond enhanced damages, the remedies in ss 96, 97, 99, 100, the
-- definitions of doxxing, false material, statements harmful to reputation and incitement of violence beyond their names, and the
-- amendments to other Acts (Part 15 and the Schedule). Anything left to regulations (prescribed connections, periods, damages
-- limits) is not known here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Online Safety (Relief and Accountability) Act 2025 -- online harms`

-- s 3(1): "online harmful activity" means (a) online harassment; (b) doxxing; (c) non-consensual disclosure of private information;
-- (d) online stalking; (e) intimate image abuse; (f) image-based child abuse; (g) online impersonation; (h) inauthentic material
-- abuse; (i) publication of false material; (j) publication of statement harmful to reputation; (k) online instigation of
-- disproportionate harm; (l) incitement of enmity; (m) incitement of violence; (n) any prescribed type (not encoded).
DECLARE Harm IS ONE OF
    `online harassment`
    `doxxing`
    `non-consensual disclosure of private information`
    `online stalking`
    `intimate image abuse`
    `image-based child abuse`
    `online impersonation`
    `inauthentic material abuse`
    `publication of false material`
    `publication of statement harmful to reputation`
    `online instigation of disproportionate harm`
    `incitement of enmity`
    `incitement of violence`

DECLARE Connection IS ONE OF
    `a citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a person with a prescribed connection`
    `a person with no connection to Singapore`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Connection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the connection to Singapore that s 22 requires` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a person with no connection to Singapore` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a harm against a group` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `incitement of enmity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `incitement of violence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 and 22 -- who may report to the Commissioner`

-- s 22(1): "A victim of an alleged online harmful activity (other than incitement of enmity and incitement of violence) who is --
-- (a) a citizen of Singapore; (b) a permanent resident of Singapore; or (c) a person who has a prescribed connection to Singapore,
-- is eligible to make a report". (2) On behalf of such a victim: "(a) where the victim is below 18 years of age, the victim's parent
-- or guardian"; (b) a prescribed person; (c) a person "whom or which the Commissioner is satisfied has obtained the written
-- authorisation or written consent". (3) Anyone with the same connection who "fulfils the requirements that are prescribed" may
-- report incitement of enmity or violence.
-- s 4(1): "A public agency may not make a report under section 22(1) or (3)", but may report on a person's behalf.
GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm, `the victim` IS A Connection, `the victim is a public agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the victim may report it` IF
        (NOT `is a harm against a group` `the harm`)
    AND `has the connection to Singapore that s 22 requires` `the victim`
    AND (NOT `the victim is a public agency`)

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm, `the victim` IS A Connection, `the victim's age` IS A NUMBER,
      `the reporter is the victim's parent or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the reporter holds written authorisation or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `another person may report it on the victim's behalf` IF
        (NOT `is a harm against a group` `the harm`)
    AND `has the connection to Singapore that s 22 requires` `the victim`
    AND (    (`the reporter is the victim's parent or guardian` AND `the victim's age` LESS THAN 18)
         OR  `the Commissioner is satisfied the reporter holds written authorisation or consent`)

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm, `the reporter` IS A Connection, `the reporter meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the reporter is a public agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a member of the public may report the incitement` IF
        `is a harm against a group` `the harm`
    AND `has the connection to Singapore that s 22 requires` `the reporter`
    AND `the reporter meets the prescribed requirements`
    AND (NOT `the reporter is a public agency`)

§§ `25 -- vexatious reporters`

-- s 25(2), (3): the Commissioner may decide that future reports by a persistent vexatious reporter, or about a matter, "will not be
-- considered"; (4) the period "must not exceed 3 years after the date of the decision"; (5) the decision "is final and not subject
-- to reconsideration or appeal".
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bar on future reports is within the permitted period` IF
    `months` AT MOST 36

§§ `26(5), (6) -- when only a right of reply may be ordered`

-- s 26(5): "Only a right-of-reply (user) direction or a right-of-reply (online service) direction may be given in respect of a
-- publication of false material ... unless the false material published contains or consists of a false statement of fact that the
-- victim -- (a) approved, endorsed, promoted, provided a testimonial for or invested in; or (b) is affiliated or associated with,
-- any genuine or purported -- (c) trade; (d) investment; (e) business; (f) commercial activity; or (g) online location soliciting
-- funding, donations or financial support." (6): only a right of reply for a "publication of statement harmful to reputation".
GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm, `the falsehood ties the victim to a trade, investment, business or fundraising` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `only a right-of-reply direction may be given` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `publication of statement harmful to reputation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `publication of false material` THEN NOT `the falsehood ties the victim to a trade, investment, business or fundraising`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `9 -- online harassment`

-- s 9(1): material "that a reasonable person would conclude is -- (a) threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent; and
-- (b) likely to cause a person ... harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation". (2) not "sexual or indecent material that has a
-- legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art". (3) A person to whom it was not directed may be a victim
-- "by reason of X's personal relationship with the person to whom the communication was directed".
GIVEN `threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sexual or indecent material with a legitimate scientific, medical, educational or artistic purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is online harassment` IF
        `threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent`
    AND `likely to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    AND (NOT `sexual or indecent material with a legitimate scientific, medical, educational or artistic purpose`)

GIVEN `it was directed at this person` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a personal relationship with the person it was directed at` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to cause this person harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a victim of the harassment` IF
        `likely to cause this person harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    AND (`it was directed at this person` OR `has a personal relationship with the person it was directed at`)

§§ `11 -- non-consensual disclosure of private information`

-- s 11(1): publication of private information "(a) ... without the victim's consent; and (b) ... likely to cause the victim
-- harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation". (2) "private information" is information "that was not, prior to the publication,
-- widely available to the public at large". (3) Not information "obtained by perceiving in public or through publicly available
-- information such as -- (a) the physical appearance of the person; or (b) the conduct or activities of the person".
GIVEN `widely available to the public before` IS A BOOLEAN, `the victim consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtained by perceiving the person in public or from public information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is non-consensual disclosure of private information` IF
        (NOT `widely available to the public before`)
    AND (NOT `the victim consented`)
    AND `likely to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    AND (NOT `obtained by perceiving the person in public or from public information`)

§§ `12(4) -- a course of online conduct`

-- s 12(4): "course of online conduct" means online conduct "(a) on one occasion, if -- (i) the conduct is protracted; or (ii) the
-- online stalker has a previous conviction under section 7 of the Protection from Harassment Act 2014 in respect of the same victim;
-- or (b) on 2 or more occasions in any other case."
GIVEN `occasions` IS A NUMBER, `the conduct is protracted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a previous POHA s 7 conviction for the same victim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a course of online conduct` IF
        `occasions` AT LEAST 2
    OR  (`occasions` EQUALS 1 AND (`the conduct is protracted` OR `has a previous POHA s 7 conviction for the same victim`))

§§ `13(2) -- intimate image or recording`

-- s 13(2): "intimate image or recording" "(a) means an image or a recording (including an image or a recording that has been altered
-- or generated by any means) -- (i) of the person's genital or anal region, whether bare or covered by underwear; (ii) of the
-- person's breasts if the person is a female, whether bare or covered by underwear; or (iii) of the person doing a private act; but
-- (b) excludes an image or a recording that no reasonable person would believe depicts that person."
-- Whether the image was altered or generated is taken as a parameter only to show that it changes nothing.
GIVEN `shows the genital or anal region` IS A BOOLEAN, `shows a female's breasts` IS A BOOLEAN, `shows a private act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was altered or generated, for example by AI` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no reasonable person would believe it depicts the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an intimate image or recording of the person` IF
        (`shows the genital or anal region` OR `shows a female's breasts` OR `shows a private act`)
    AND (NOT `no reasonable person would believe it depicts the person`)

§§ `14 -- image-based child abuse`

-- s 14(2): a child abuse image is one of a person "who is, or appears to a reasonable person to be, or who is implied to be, below
-- 16 years of age". (3) Not material that "(a) has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art; and
-- (b) does not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age".
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `appears to be below 16` IS A BOOLEAN, `is implied to be below 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person depicted is a child for s 14` IF
    `age` LESS THAN 16 OR `appears to be below 16` OR `is implied to be below 16`

GIVEN `contains a child abuse image or recording` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a legitimate purpose` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `poses an undue risk of harm to under-16s` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is image-based child abuse` IF
        `contains a child abuse image or recording`
    AND (NOT (`has a legitimate purpose` AND (NOT `poses an undue risk of harm to under-16s`)))

§§ `15, 16 -- impersonation and inauthentic material`

-- s 15: online impersonation "(a) involves X pretending to be the victim without the victim's consent; and (b) would lead a
-- reasonable person to believe that the online activity was conducted by the victim". Explanation: parody or satire "which no
-- reasonable person would believe is made by a person is not online impersonation".
-- s 16(2): inauthentic material is "(a) ... altered or generated using digital means; (b) ... a false or misleading depiction ... of
-- the victim's words, actions or conduct, even though the victim may not appear in the material; and (c) ... realistic enough such
-- that a reasonable person would believe" it. Illustration (b): a prominent AI label can make it not realistic enough.
GIVEN `pretends to be the victim without consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reasonable person would believe it was the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is online impersonation` IF
    `pretends to be the victim without consent` AND `a reasonable person would believe it was the victim`

GIVEN `digitally altered or generated` IS A BOOLEAN, `falsely depicts the victim's words or conduct` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `realistic enough to be believed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is inauthentic material` IF
    `digitally altered or generated` AND `falsely depicts the victim's words or conduct` AND `realistic enough to be believed`

§§ `19(4), 87(7) -- political responses are outside instigation`

-- s 19(4) (and s 87(7) for the tort): the section "does not apply where the act or omission that the statement tends to instigate is
-- any of the following: (a) voting for any candidate in an election ...; (b) conducting or otherwise participating in or attending a
-- political activity; (c) communicating a statement calling for the removal or suspension of a political office holder or Member of
-- Parliament ...; (d) communicating a statement to a political office holder, a Member of Parliament or a public body on a matter of
-- public interest or public controversy."
DECLARE Response IS ONE OF
    `voting against a candidate`
    `attending a political rally`
    `calling for a Minister to resign`
    `writing to an MP about it`
    `flooding the victim's employer with complaints`
    `turning up at the victim's home`

GIVEN `the response` IS A Response
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instigation provisions can apply to` IF
    CONSIDER `the response`
    WHEN `voting against a candidate` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `attending a political rally` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `calling for a Minister to resign` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `writing to an MP about it` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `20 -- incitement of enmity`

-- s 20(1): material a reasonable person "would conclude incites, or is likely to incite, feelings of enmity, hatred or hostility
-- against any group in Singapore". (2) Not communication "private or domestic in nature", nor where "the parties to the communication
-- desire it to be heard, seen or otherwise perceived only by themselves". (3) Not satisfied "solely because one or more persons feel
-- offended by or uncomfortable with the material".
GIVEN `a reasonable person would conclude it incites enmity against a group` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `private or domestic in nature` IS A BOOLEAN, `meant only for the parties themselves` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the only effect is that people feel offended or uncomfortable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is incitement of enmity` IF
        `a reasonable person would conclude it incites enmity against a group`
    AND (NOT `the only effect is that people feel offended or uncomfortable`)
    AND (NOT `private or domestic in nature`)
    AND (NOT `meant only for the parties themselves`)

§§ `69, 71, 72, 73 -- offences and maximum penalties`

-- s 71(1): an offence if the person "(a) is given any Part 5 direction; and (b) without reasonable excuse, fails to comply"; (2) an
-- individual: "$20,000 or ... 12 months or ... both and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... $2,000 for every day"; otherwise
-- "$500,000 and ... $50,000 for every day".
-- s 73(1): "It is not a defence ... that -- (a) the person is subject to a duty of confidentiality ... or (b) the person has applied
-- for a reconsideration of, or has appealed against, the relevant direction". (3) It is a defence if the accused proves "(a) it was
-- not reasonably practicable to do more than what was in fact done to comply".
GIVEN `was given a Part 5 direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved it was not reasonably practicable to do more` IS A BOOLEAN, `has applied for reconsideration or appealed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owes a duty of confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to comply with the direction is an offence` IF
        `was given a Part 5 direction`
    AND (NOT `complied`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND (NOT `proved it was not reasonably practicable to do more`)

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for not complying with a Part 5 direction` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 20000 ELSE 500000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further daily fine for not complying with a Part 5 direction` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 2000 ELSE 50000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for not complying with a Part 5 direction` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 12 ELSE 0

-- s 72(2): access blocking order, "$250,000 and ... $20,000 for every day"; (4) app removal order, "$500,000 and ... $50,000 for
-- every day". No distinction between individuals and others.
DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `an access blocking order`
    `an app removal order`

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for not complying with the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `an access blocking order` THEN 250000
    OTHERWISE 500000

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further daily fine for not complying with the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `an access blocking order` THEN 20000
    OTHERWISE 50000

-- s 69(1), (2): false or misleading information in a report, application or investigation, known, ought reasonably to be known or
-- reckless: an individual "$20,000 or ... 12 months or ... both"; otherwise "$50,000". (4) not if not false or misleading "in a
-- material particular".
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for false information to the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 20000 ELSE 50000

§§ `83 to 88 -- statutory torts against the person who did it`

-- Part 10 creates torts for intimate image abuse (s 83), image-based child abuse (s 84), online impersonation (s 85), inauthentic
-- material abuse (s 86), online instigation of disproportionate harm (s 87) and incitement of violence (s 88), and no others.
GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 10 gives a tort against the wrongdoer for` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `intimate image abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `image-based child abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `online impersonation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `inauthentic material abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `online instigation of disproportionate harm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `incitement of violence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 83(3): defences for X to prove: "(a) that X's conduct was reasonable; (b) that X had reasonable grounds to believe that the victim
-- consented ...; or (c) that X did not know and had no reason to suspect that the material ... was an intimate image or recording."
GIVEN `communicated intimate image abuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved reasonable grounds to believe the victim consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no reason to suspect it was an intimate image` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is liable in tort for intimate image abuse` IF
        `communicated intimate image abuse`
    AND (NOT `proved the conduct was reasonable`)
    AND (NOT `proved reasonable grounds to believe the victim consented`)
    AND (NOT `proved no reason to suspect it was an intimate image`)

-- s 84(2): the victim "who was below 16 years of age at the time the victim was depicted" may sue. (3) defences: "(a) that X's
-- conduct was reasonable; or (b) that X did not know and had no reason to suspect". There is no consent defence; a belief in consent
-- is taken as a parameter only to show that it changes nothing.
GIVEN `communicated image-based child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `the victim's age when depicted` IS A NUMBER,
      `proved the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no reason to suspect it was a child abuse image` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `believed the victim consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the victim may recover for image-based child abuse` IF
        `communicated image-based child abuse`
    AND `the victim's age when depicted` LESS THAN 16
    AND (NOT `proved the conduct was reasonable`)
    AND (NOT `proved no reason to suspect it was a child abuse image`)

-- s 85(1): no online impersonation "if the online activity is likely to cause a victim harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation";
-- (3) defences: conduct reasonable, or reasonable grounds to believe the victim consented.
GIVEN `conducted online impersonation` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable grounds to believe the victim consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is liable in tort for online impersonation` IF
        `conducted online impersonation`
    AND `likely to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    AND (NOT `proved the conduct was reasonable`)
    AND (NOT `proved reasonable grounds to believe the victim consented`)

-- s 86(1): communicating "material that X knew or had reasonable grounds to believe was inauthentic material of a victim"; (3) the
-- same two defences as s 85.
GIVEN `communicated inauthentic material abuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or had reason to believe it was inauthentic` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable grounds to believe the victim consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is liable in tort for inauthentic material abuse` IF
        `communicated inauthentic material abuse`
    AND `knew or had reason to believe it was inauthentic`
    AND (NOT `proved the conduct was reasonable`)
    AND (NOT `proved reasonable grounds to believe the victim consented`)

-- s 87(4): "X is not liable if X proves that -- (a) the statement did not in fact cause the loss and damage ...; (b) it was not
-- reasonably foreseeable that the statement would instigate the act or omission ...; or (c) X had acted reasonably". (7): not where
-- the instigated response is political (see s 19(4) above).
GIVEN `the statement meets s 87(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the response` IS A Response, `proved the statement did not cause the loss` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the response was not reasonably foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved X acted reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is liable in tort for online instigation` IF
        `the statement meets s 87(1)`
    AND `the instigation provisions can apply to` `the response`
    AND (NOT `proved the statement did not cause the loss`)
    AND (NOT `proved the response was not reasonably foreseeable`)
    AND (NOT `proved X acted reasonably`)

-- s 88(3): "it is a defence for X to prove that X's conduct was reasonable"; (4) "each member of the group against which the unlawful
-- force or unlawful violence is incited ... is a victim".
GIVEN `communicated incitement of violence` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a member of the targeted group` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this person may sue for incitement of violence` IF
        `communicated incitement of violence`
    AND `is a member of the targeted group`
    AND (NOT `proved the conduct was reasonable`)

§§ `89, 91, 92 -- administrators and online harm notices`

-- s 89(1) (and s 93(1) for online service providers): Part 11 "applies only to" online harassment, doxxing, online stalking, intimate
-- image abuse, image-based child abuse, online impersonation, inauthentic material abuse and incitement of violence.
GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an online harm notice can be sent for` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `online harassment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `doxxing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `online stalking` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `intimate image abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `image-based child abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `online impersonation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `inauthentic material abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `incitement of violence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 91(6): "it is presumed until the contrary is proved that the respondent failed to take the reasonable steps ... if the victim
-- proves that -- (a) an online harm notice was sent ... in accordance with subsections (1) and (2); (b) the applicable online harmful
-- activity ... occurred at the online location administered by the respondent; (c) [it] involved the communication of online
-- material; and (d) after a reasonable period of time had passed ..., that online material was not removed".
GIVEN `a proper notice was sent` IS A BOOLEAN, `the harm occurred at the administrator's location` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the harm involved online material` IS A BOOLEAN, `the material was still up after a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the administrator is presumed to have failed to take reasonable steps` IF
        `a proper notice was sent`
    AND `the harm occurred at the administrator's location`
    AND `the harm involved online material`
    AND `the material was still up after a reasonable time`

-- s 91(5): the person who "(a) sent the online harm notice in accordance with subsections (1) and (2); and (b) is a victim" may sue;
-- (7) "it is a defence for the respondent to prove that, through no fault of the respondent, the respondent did not receive the
-- online harm notice".
GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm, `the claimant sent a proper notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claimant is the victim` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the administrator failed its duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved the notice was not received through no fault of its own` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the administrator is liable for failing to respond to the notice` IF
        `an online harm notice can be sent for` `the harm`
    AND `the claimant sent a proper notice`
    AND `the claimant is the victim`
    AND `the administrator failed its duty`
    AND (NOT `proved the notice was not received through no fault of its own`)

-- s 92: the administrator "has a right of action ... against Z if Z sent an online harm notice ... and the online harm notice --
-- (a) is frivolous; or (b) is false in a material way and which Z knew to be false".
GIVEN `the notice was frivolous` IS A BOOLEAN, `the notice was materially false` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sender knew it was false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the administrator may sue the sender of the notice` IF
    `the notice was frivolous` OR (`the notice was materially false` AND `the sender knew it was false`)

§§ `98 -- enhanced damages`

-- s 98(1): in Part 10 proceedings (and (2), a s 90(3) claim) the court may award enhanced damages where "(a) the victim made a
-- reasonable written request to the respondent ... to address the online harmful activity ...; and (b) the respondent failed, without
-- reasonable excuse, to address the online harmful activity within a reasonable time." (3) In addition to general and special damages.
GIVEN `the claim is under Part 10 or section 90(3)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the victim made a reasonable written request` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the respondent addressed it within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the respondent had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `enhanced damages may be awarded` IF
        `the claim is under Part 10 or section 90(3)`
    AND `the victim made a reasonable written request`
    AND (NOT `the respondent addressed it within a reasonable time`)
    AND (NOT `the respondent had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `101, 102, 106 -- place, contract terms and the Family Court`

-- s 101: a Part 10, 11 or 12 tort is treated as taking place in Singapore if an element "(a) was initiated or occurred in or from
-- Singapore; (b) is perceived by one or more persons in Singapore; or (c) caused damage, loss or harm suffered in Singapore."
GIVEN `initiated in or from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `perceived by someone in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `caused harm suffered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tort is treated as taking place in Singapore` IF
    `initiated in or from Singapore` OR `perceived by someone in Singapore` OR `caused harm suffered in Singapore`

-- s 102(1): a term is void to the extent "(a) it is inconsistent with Part 11 or 12; (b) it purports to exclude or limit the
-- jurisdiction of the courts of Singapore for a claim made under Part 11 or 12; or (c) it purports to prevent a person from making a
-- claim under Part 11 or 12". (2) Not a term "that is fair and reasonable".
GIVEN `inconsistent with Part 11 or 12` IS A BOOLEAN, `ousts the Singapore courts for a Part 11 or 12 claim` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prevents a Part 11 or 12 claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `fair and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract term is void` IF
        (`inconsistent with Part 11 or 12` OR `ousts the Singapore courts for a Part 11 or 12 claim` OR `prevents a Part 11 or 12 claim`)
    AND (NOT `fair and reasonable`)

-- s 106(1): "Any Part 10 proceedings may be commenced in the first instance in a Family Court, in which any related family
-- proceedings are pending, with the permission of that court." (6)(b) "Part 10 proceedings" means proceedings "seeking relief under
-- section 99 or 100 (excluding proceedings seeking relief under section 96, 97 or 98)" -- that is, not damages.
GIVEN `related family proceedings are pending there` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Family Court gives permission` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the claim seeks damages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Part 10 claim may start in the Family Court` IF
        `related family proceedings are pending there`
    AND `the Family Court gives permission`
    AND (NOT `the claim seeks damages`)
